Jahshaka patch 0040 — export Ogre::onVulkanFailure, so the Vulkan render
system's own PUBLIC accessors can be linked against from outside the plugin.

WHY (Photon lane R1; SPECS/PHOTON_SPEC.md §7 R1). A pin defect, found by
building against the pin exactly as its installed headers invite.

THE DEFECT. VulkanQueue is declared `class _OgreVulkanExport VulkanQueue`
(OgreVulkanQueue.h:43) — i.e. deliberately visible outside the plugin — and it
offers a PUBLIC INLINE accessor in that installed public header:

    VkCommandBuffer getCurrentCmdBuffer()
    {
        if( !mCurrentCmdBuffer )  // device lost ...
            checkVkResult( mOwnerDevice, VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST, "getCurrentCmdBuffer" );
        return mCurrentCmdBuffer;
    }
                                        (OgreVulkanQueue.h:223-228)

`checkVkResult` expands to a call to `Ogre::onVulkanFailure`, and THAT function
is declared with no export macro at all (OgreVulkanPrerequisites.h:150). The
Vulkan render system builds with `-fvisibility=hidden` (the `#else` branch at
OgreVulkanPrerequisites.h:192 defines `_OgreVulkanExport` as
`visibility("hidden")` for everything not explicitly exported), so the symbol is
absent from RenderSystem_Vulkan.so's dynamic table:

    $ nm -D --defined-only lib/OGRE-Next/RenderSystem_Vulkan.so | grep -c onVulkanFailure
    0
    $ nm -D --defined-only lib/OGRE-Next/RenderSystem_Vulkan.so | grep endAllEncoders
    T Ogre::VulkanQueue::endAllEncoders(bool)

The consequence: any code outside the plugin that calls the pin's own exported,
public, header-inline accessor COMPILES and then fails to LINK with

    undefined reference to `Ogre::onVulkanFailure(Ogre::VulkanDevice*, int,
      const char*, const char*, const char*, long)'

That is not a Jahshaka problem to work around — it is the pin advertising an API
it does not export the whole of. Every out-of-line entry point of the same class
(`endAllEncoders`, `getComputeEncoder`, `VulkanRenderSystem::flushCommands`) IS
exported and links fine; only the inline ones that can fail are unusable.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES. Puts `_OgreVulkanExport` on the declaration of
`onVulkanFailure`, and MOVES that declaration (with the `checkVkResult` macro
that calls it) from the middle of the file to the bottom — because upstream
defines `_OgreVulkanExport` itself at the very END of this header, below where
the function was declared, so the macro does not exist yet at the old position
(`error: '_OgreVulkanExport' does not name a type`). Every other header gets the
macro fine: they include this one, by which time the whole file has been read.

No behaviour change of any kind: the function's definition is untouched, its
callers inside the plugin are untouched, the macro expansion is identical, and on
Windows `_OgreVulkanExport` is the dllexport/dllimport pair the rest of the render
system already uses. It makes the pin's public API linkable as declared.

WHY NOT A WORKAROUND. The alternative was to read `VulkanQueue::mCurrentCmdBuffer`
directly — but that member is PROTECTED (OgreVulkanQueue.h:117-118), so reaching
it means a derived-class reach-in into the render system's internals, which lives
only as long as the pin's layout does. A patch beats a workaround (owner,
2026-09-15): this one fixes the defect itself, is refused loudly by a pin bump if
upstream moves the declaration, and costs one line.

UPSTREAM. Worth reporting as-is: the same class of defect exists for every
`checkVkResult` inside a public inline in an installed Vulkan header.

SOURCE patch: every tree re-runs ./irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh.

diff --git a/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/OgreVulkanPrerequisites.h b/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/OgreVulkanPrerequisites.h
index e2298ca6e..99e689816 100644
--- a/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/OgreVulkanPrerequisites.h
+++ b/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/OgreVulkanPrerequisites.h
@@ -147,20 +147,8 @@ namespace Ogre
         };
     }
 
-    void onVulkanFailure( VulkanDevice *device, int result, const char *message, const char *func,
-                          const char *file, long line );
 }  // namespace Ogre
 
-#define checkVkResult( device, result, functionName ) \
-    do \
-    { \
-        if( result != VK_SUCCESS ) \
-        { \
-            onVulkanFailure( device, result, functionName " failed", OGRE_CURRENT_FUNCTION, __FILE__, \
-                             __LINE__ ); \
-        } \
-    } while( 0 )
-
 #if OGRE_PLATFORM == OGRE_PLATFORM_WIN32
 #    if !defined( __MINGW32__ )
 #        define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
@@ -195,4 +183,28 @@ namespace Ogre
 #    define _OgreVulkanExport
 #endif
 
+// Jahshaka (ogre-patch 0040): onVulkanFailure MUST be declared after
+// _OgreVulkanExport is defined, and it must carry it. VulkanQueue is an exported
+// class whose PUBLIC INLINE getCurrentCmdBuffer() expands checkVkResult(), so
+// every caller outside the plugin emits a reference to this symbol - and without
+// the export macro the render system's -fvisibility=hidden keeps it out of
+// RenderSystem_Vulkan.so's dynamic table, making the pin's own public accessor
+// impossible to LINK against. The declaration moved down here from its old place
+// above (where the macro does not exist yet); nothing else changed.
+namespace Ogre
+{
+    _OgreVulkanExport void onVulkanFailure( VulkanDevice *device, int result, const char *message,
+                                            const char *func, const char *file, long line );
+}  // namespace Ogre
+
+#define checkVkResult( device, result, functionName ) \
+    do \
+    { \
+        if( result != VK_SUCCESS ) \
+        { \
+            onVulkanFailure( device, result, functionName " failed", OGRE_CURRENT_FUNCTION, __FILE__, \
+                             __LINE__ ); \
+        } \
+    } while( 0 )
+
 #endif  // #ifndef _OgreVulkanPrerequisites_H_
